<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan issues decree for stocks depository.</title>
<headline>Pakistan issues decree for stocks depository.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Farooq Leghari issued a decree on Tuesday providing a legal framework for setting up a central depository system (CDS) for Pakistan's stock market, the official APP news agency reported.</p>
<p>Details of the ordinance were not immediately available. But stock market officials have said in the past the system, due to be installed at the main Karachi Stock Exchange soon after the start of planned computerised trading, would improve the trading and settlement system.</p>
<p>The sponsors of the $3.5 million CDS project are the Karachi, Lahore and Islamabad stock exchanges, the International Finance Corporation, Citibank, Muslim Commercial Bank, Habib Bank Ltd, National Investment Trust, Investment Corp of Pakistan and Pakistan Industrial Credit and Investment Corp.</p>
